### 3.1 Estimating the Magnitude of Completeness  
Seismostats provides three methods to estimate the **magnitude of completeness** ($M_c$) in earthquake catalogs:  
- **Maximum Curvature**
- **b-Stability**
- **Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) Test**  
These methods help assess the quality of your catalog by identifying the lowest magnitude above which events are reliably recorded. More information on the methods can be found in the section `Magnitude of Completeness`.  
